<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-May non-CIS oil, product exports jump.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-May non-CIS oil, product exports jump.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia exported 44.55 million tonnes (2.14 million barrels per day) of oil to countries outside the Commonwealth of Independent States in the first five months of 1997, up 12 percent from year-ago levels, the State Statistics Committee said on Friday.</p>
<p>Non-CIS oil product exports rose 20 percent in January-May to 22.42 million tonnes against 18.60 million in the first five months of 1996, the committee, quoted by Interfax news agency, said.  </p>
<p>Russia's non-CIS natural gas exports fell to 51.80 billion cubic metres (bcm) in the first five months of 1997, down six percent from 54.90 bcm in the same year-ago period.</p>
<p>The committee gave the following data for energy exports.</p>
<p>	  RUSSIAN JAN-MAY 1997 NON-CIS ENERGY EXPORTS</p>
<p>			 Jan-May	   Jan-May     pct change</p>
<p>				 1997	  1996	  yr/yr</p>
<p> Crude oil (million T)	  44.55	39.90	 +12</p>
<p> Oil products (million T)     22.42	18.60	 +20</p>
<p> Natural gas (bcm)		51.80	54.90	 -6</p>
<p>Electricity</p>
<p>  (bln kilowatt hours)     2.68	    3.82    -30</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 9520</p>
</text>
